{
  "id": "Compound::DB01222 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Budesonide, a corticosteroid hormone receptor agonist, is linked to Cyp3a4 through multiple pathways that converge on the therapeutic glucocorticoid class. The evidence suggests that Budesonide, through its inclusion in corticosteroid hormone receptor agonists, binds to Cyp3a4 in a manner that is consistent with the broader biological context of glucocorticoid action. This is supported by the presence of multiple related compounds—such as cortisone acetate, triamcinolone, and prednisolone—each of which exhibits a binding interaction with Cyp3a4, reinforcing the role of the enzyme in metabolizing steroid hormones. The lowest common ancestors of these compounds, including the therapeutic glucocorticoid class, further suggest a shared mechanism of action that involves the enzyme Cyp3a4. The evidence is robust and consistent, with multiple independent pathways converging on the same core mechanism, indicating a well-defined relationship between Budesonide and Cyp3a4.",
